// A section of chalk cliff about 50 m across and 60 m high: white, fluted down its face
// by the rain into broad rounded ribs and narrow grooves, a few deep gullies, faint bands
// of flint across it, grey streaks and green where plants have taken the ledges, rounded
// over at the top where the turf begins. Set several side by side, overlapping, into a
// step in the ground: the ends tuck back so the next one hides the join.
// Any number in shape, surface, moss or face may be a (lo, hi) range: each seed lands in it.
